=== width 80, default
\e[1m\e[3m\e[4:2mfrobnicate\e[24m\e[23m\e[22m

A small command line tool that \e[1mfrobnicates\e[22m files, \e[3mquickly\e[23m and with \e[38;5;3mzero\e[39m
configuration. See \e[4mhttps://example.com/frobnicate\e[24m for the full manual, or ask in
the chat.

\e[1m\e[4mInstallation\e[24m\e[22m

Install from source with a recent Rust toolchain:

  cargo install frobnicate
  frobnicate\e[38;5;6m --version\e[39m

Prebuilt binaries are available for these platforms:

• Linux, x86_64 and aarch64
• macOS, Apple silicon and Intel
• Windows, x86_64 only
  • requires the Visual C++ runtime
  • no ARM build yet

\e[1m\e[4mUsage\e[24m\e[22m

  \e[38;5;3mfrobnicate [OPTIONS] <FILE>...\e[39m

┌─────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────┐
│ \e[1m  Option   \e[22m │ \e[1m               Meaning                \e[22m │ \e[1mDefault\e[22m │
├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────┤
│ \e[38;5;3m-q\e[39m, \e[38;5;3m--quiet\e[39m │ Print nothing except errors            │   off   │
├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────┤
│ \e[38;5;3m-j\e[39m, \e[38;5;3m--jobs\e[39m  │ Number of parallel jobs                │    \e[38;5;3m4\e[39m    │
├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────┤
│ \e[38;5;3m--dry-run\e[39m   │ Show what would change, change nothing │   off   │
└─────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────┘

\e[1mExit codes\e[22m

1. \e[38;5;3m0\e[39m when every file was processed.
2. \e[38;5;3m1\e[39m when at least one file failed.
3. \e[38;5;3m2\e[39m for invalid arguments.

\e[38;5;6m│ \e[39m\e[1mNote\e[22m Frobnication is not reversible. Keep a backup, or use \e[38;5;3m--dry-run\e[39m first.

\e[1m\e[4mConfiguration\e[24m\e[22m

Settings live in \e[38;5;3mfrobnicate.toml\e[39m:

  [\e[38;5;3mdefaults\e[39m]
  \e[38;5;1mjobs\e[39m = \e[38;5;3m8\e[39m
  \e[38;5;1mquiet\e[39m = \e[38;5;3mfalse\e[39m

\e[1m\e[4mContributing\e[24m\e[22m

Pull requests are welcome. Please run the tests first, and mention the issue
number in the title. For larger changes, open an issue to discuss the idea.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Released under the MIT license. Copyright (c) the frobnicate authors.
